            <div xml:id="d634">

                <pb facs="0769" n="625" sameAs="frus:frus1929v02/pg625"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">711.933/171: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >MacMurray</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peiping</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1929-11-20T18:00:00+08:00">November 20, 1929—6
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received November 21—2:55 a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>1014. My 1009, November 19, 6 p.m., last paragraph. Following from American
                    Consul at Nanking: <pb facs="0770" n="626" xml:id="pg626"/>
                    <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“November 19, 12 p.m. Wang informed me tonight that, knowing that the
                            American Minister was leaving Peiping, he had telegraphed his views, in
                            reply to the American extraterritoriality note of November 1st, to
                            Chinese Minister in Washington for communication to Department of
                            State.”</p>
                    </quote></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">MacMurray</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
